Hi @AbdElrahman-Rafaat-Amer,
The purpose of Secrets Vault is to store keys inside the final application (APK) securely. Build scripts (build.gradle files) are not included directly inside the final APK, but the code produced by them are. Hence, actually it should be fine not to secure keys used only on build/compile time unless you share your project's source code publicly.
If you still need to secure keys that is only used on build/compile time, you can store them as environment variables.
Note that if the keys are not used only on build/compile time, i.e., they are included inside the final APK, you should set them on runtime via Secrets Vault instead of build/compile time:
So, instead of doing:
someSDK {
  apiKey = "..."
}

You should do:
class MyApplication : Application() {
  override fun onCreate() {
    SomeSDK.setApiKey(MainSecrets().getSomeSDKApiKey())
  }
}

